    {
      "source": "hackernews",
      "subsource": "news.ycombinator.com",
      "category": "ai",
      "title": "Publish fake stats, get cited in LLMs",
      "url": "https://peec.ai/blog/publish-stats-get-cited-the-tactic-that-put-my-data-all-over-the-web",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50165801",
      "score": 344,
      "comments": 198,
      "author": "robtherobber",
      "published": "2026-10-20T13:06:22Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Web-grounded LLMs and RAG systems readily ingest and amplify fabricated web statistics due to reliance on unverified search index results.",
        "Search engines and models like ChatGPT or Perplexity lack epistemic verification, treating indexed, SEO-optimized fake citations as authoritative ground truth.",
        "Defenses require source-reputation scoring, cross-domain consensus validation, and strict provenance tracking in downstream retrieval pipelines to mitigate deliberate poisoning."
      ]
    },
